Operator asked for OTHER research papers / options after the score stayed flat. Ran a fresh 4-scout
WebSearch/WebFetch sweep over paradigm families NOT previously ingested (unsupervised skill discovery;
intrinsic/empowerment/active-inference exploration; learned-neural latent world models; open-ended
curriculum/library transfer + new ARC-AGI-3 papers), filtered against the information-theoretic wall +
our offline/weak-9B/tiny-data constraints. Real arXiv IDs.

HONEST VERDICT: no method escapes the wall. Every intrinsic/skill/WM/curriculum objective is computed
over already-sampled observable experience -> can only re-rank/recompose it (the nulled exp4893 class).
The one flagged exception (active-inference EFE pragmatic goal-prior) reduces to the already-nulled
exp4640 (goal-energy directs generation, 0/100 solved) -- same signal, no generative escape.

DECISIVE NEW INPUT (not previously ingested): the official ARC-AGI-3 tech report (arXiv:2603.24621)
shows the preview WINNER (StochasticGoose/Tufa, 12.58%) collapsed to 0.25% on the full unseen set,
indistinguishable from frontier LLMs (Gemini-3.1-Pro 0.37%, GPT-5.4 0.26%); only 2/8 agents solved >1
game; winners used 'smart-random', not structure-learning. Independent confirmation that the generation
wall is UNIVERSAL -- nobody has cracked generalizable first-contact -- and that Carnot's standing 0.08
is genuinely competitive. Winner code: github.com/DriesSmit/ARC3-solution.

OPTIONS (ranked, honest): (1) accept the wall, ship 0.08 + FoVer paper [highest confidence]; (2) study
the winner's code for a possible offline-reproducible-level / efficiency lift (secondary, no wall-break);
(3) paradigm change outside our constraints (offline-illegal strong inducer / bigger local model) --
bounded, since even neural-online-RL winners collapsed.

